## User Data

The EC2 instance automatically installs and starts Nginx during initial boot.

```bash
#!/bin/bash

dnf update -y
dnf install -y nginx

systemctl enable nginx
systemctl start nginx

cat > /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html <<'EOF'
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Reliability Lab</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>AWS Reliability & Automation Lab</h1>
    <p>Nginx is running successfully.</p>
    <p>Project: ReliabilityLab</p>
</body>
</html>
EOF
```

## Security Configuration

The EC2 security group uses:

| Protocol | Port | Source              | Purpose               |
| -------- | ---: | ------------------- | --------------------- |
| HTTP     |   80 | `0.0.0.0/0`         | Public web access     |
| SSH      |   22 | Administrator IP/32 | Administrative access |

SSH is restricted to the administrator's IP rather than being exposed to the entire Internet.

## Cost Protection

An AWS Budget was created before deploying the workload.

Configuration:

```text
Monthly Budget: $5
Alerting: Email notification
```

The budget provides cost monitoring for the lab. It does not automatically terminate resources.

